<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35643" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-transĕo</span></b> , īvi,
			īre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to go</i> or <i>pass
			through</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum viridis aspectus (smaragdi), non
					pertransit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					37, 5, 18, § 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gen. 12, 6</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>To go</i> or <i>pass by</i> (late
			Lat.; not in <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 4, 3</span></i>),
				<i><span class="en">Hier. in Isa. 8, 26, v. 19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Levita, cum esset secus locum et videret eum,
					pertransiit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Luc. 10, 32</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>To pass away</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">donec pertranseat indignatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 26, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
